   "k": "j6k4di",
   "en": "Strategies and guides"
  },
  {
   "k": "1345498",
   "en": "The below is ⟦0⟧ player suggested strategies for ⟦1⟧. Bear in mind, due to the dynamic nature of the game, it may unfold differently for other players.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "19pak2x",
   "en": "A Turkic-Chinese Union"
  },
  {
   "k": "40ft3t",
   "en": "Sinkiang has the unique ability to proclaim Turkestan after conquering the \"Stans\" that are in the USSR as well as core all of China. This, along with a starting party of communism, makes Sinkiang (Xinjiang) distinct from other warlords. But with the least population and only one free building slot for another factory in the entirety of Sinkiang, it will be quite an uphill battle."
  },
  {
   "k": "cbu0kw",
   "en": "Independent action; Opposition and Border Conflicts"
  },
  {
   "k": "ck5nd8",
   "en": "First finish \"Secure Internal Politics\" and \"Opposition\". Prepare 6 divisions (the number of units drawn into border conflicts) that are optimized for high soft attack to win border conflicts quickly; or at least what one may scrounge together before Japan performs Marco Polo. Do not go to war with Japan. Immediately justify war against Xibei San Ma while quickly speeding through the Border Conflict focuses to be able to do border conflicts with the Nationalists. Once the justification is complete, go to war. Upon winning, begin border conflicts with the Nationalists to ensure a direct line to the Yunnan Clique then to Guangxi by extension. Occupy them for resources while also attempting to encircle Nationalist China to prevent the Japanese from potentially capitulating them, as the Japanese should not have military access through you. Be warned: the state where a border conflict happens is somewhat random, and several unlucky happenings may leave the player with just a small share of the China pie in the end, and you'll have to fight longer for the rest."
  },
  {
   "k": "1ygzaof",
   "en": "The Soviet \"patronage\""
  },
  {
   "k": "81hzt7",
   "en": "While seemingly the weakest warlord, Sinkiang has one key advantage of not being non-aligned as with the other warlords. This allows justification of war regardless of world tension and makes it possible to join Comintern at start. Since the USSR has no interest whatsoever to any Chinese territory, you can justify on other warlords and have the USSR win the wars for you, and claim the land for free. One may also beg for the equipment desperately needed, though the Soviet Union tends to have a large equipment deficit, so you may have to resort for guns from elsewhere, such as Germany after the Anchluss."
  },
  {
   "k": "15sjlge",
   "en": "Starting as Communist also has the advantage of being able to replace Communist China by going through the ⟦0⟧ instead of the parallel Warlord Communist branch of the focus tree. This way, you are not forced to give the USSR a tribute, nor worry about giving them a war goal on you should you decide to default on it.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "10hf6cf",
   "en": "Opposition branch"
  },
  {
   "k": "r9xx7t",
   "en": "Forming the Turkic Union"
  },
  {
   "k": "ukctfr",
   "en": "With as much of China under the player's control for manpower, resources and industry, it becomes time to took at the Soviet Union if one wishes to maximise cores. By the time one finishes unifying China, if the game is set on Historical focuses, the German Reich may be preparing or are undertaking Operation Barbarossa, in which case the player should be prepared to rush in and gobble up as much of Central Asia as possible. An ideal time to strike may be about two years in or if the Germans approach Moscow or the Caucuses mountains."
  },
  {
   "k": "14wwf8m",
   "en": "Should the game deviate from the historical timepoints, it may be advisable to let the USSR or its successor state (should it have split in the civil war) slog its way through the Gobi Desert and fight a defensive attritional warfare with copious artillery and anti-air before making a final counterattack with advanced tanks."
  },
